       "description": "Reference: the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) standalone kernels/cldfra_driver of the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, which calls cal_cldfra1 EXTRACTED VERBATIM from phys/module_radiation_driver.F at build time (kernels/Makefile rule cldfra_kernels.F90), so the reference cannot drift from the model code. Inputs are the dumped t3d, p3d, qv3d, qc3d, qi3d and qs3d of the column named below (single-precision values widened), narrowed to a one-column tile by tools/prep_cldfra_dumps.py. The scheme is a pure diagnostic (no time step), so no small-dt replay is involved and no dt sensitivity applies. Why the real64 replay and not the CLDFRA the model itself wrote: the Randall branch divides the condensate by (RHGRID QVS_WEIGHT - QV)^GAMMA, a cancellation of two near-equal numbers, and near saturation that costs WRF's single-precision arithmetic up to 5.1e-5 absolute -- 1.2e-4 relative -- which is far coarser than the rel 1e-5 contract for real32 references. Evaluating this component's own expressions in binary32 reproduces the in-model CLDFRA to 6.0e-8 absolute, so the gap is WRF's arithmetic and not the transcription. Against the real64 kernel the residual is binary64 roundoff (measured over all five regimes: <= 4.3e-16 absolute in cldfra), so the column tolerances are abs 1e-12 -- about 1e-12 of the field's unit range and roughly a thousand times the measured error -- and the spot checks rel 1e-9, the double-precision contract. The `branch` column is the Fortran's cldfra1_flag and is exact. Assertions: Linf_error of the whole cldfra and branch columns against the inline reference, plus spot checks of cldfra at every layer the scheme returns a strictly fractional value for. Regime: the idealized supercell em_quarter_ss reference case (mp = 6, ra_lw = 1, 59 layers, ztop = 12800 m; the same case that supplies the RRTM warm and mixed-phase cloud-optics tests), longwave call 61, tile column 20. A PURE LIQUID cloud: six layers of cloud water at 10-15 with no ice and no snow at all, so the condensate weight is exactly 0 and the phase blend reduces to the over-WATER Murray fit -- the only case here that exercises that arm on its own. No layer reaches RHGRID, so all six are on the Randall fit (branch 3), 0.423 to 0.988, and the other 53 layers are cloud-free.",
