       "description": "Reference: the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) standalone kernels/cldfra_driver of the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, which calls cal_cldfra1 EXTRACTED VERBATIM from phys/module_radiation_driver.F at build time (kernels/Makefile rule cldfra_kernels.F90), so the reference cannot drift from the model code. Inputs are the dumped t3d, p3d, qv3d, qc3d, qi3d and qs3d of the column named below (single-precision values widened), narrowed to a one-column tile by tools/prep_cldfra_dumps.py. The scheme is a pure diagnostic (no time step), so no small-dt replay is involved and no dt sensitivity applies. Why the real64 replay and not the CLDFRA the model itself wrote: the Randall branch divides the condensate by (RHGRID QVS_WEIGHT - QV)^GAMMA, a cancellation of two near-equal numbers, and near saturation that costs WRF's single-precision arithmetic up to 5.1e-5 absolute -- 1.2e-4 relative -- which is far coarser than the rel 1e-5 contract for real32 references. Evaluating this component's own expressions in binary32 reproduces the in-model CLDFRA to 6.0e-8 absolute, so the gap is WRF's arithmetic and not the transcription. Against the real64 kernel the residual is binary64 roundoff (measured over all five regimes: <= 4.3e-16 absolute in cldfra), so the column tolerances are abs 1e-12 -- about 1e-12 of the field's unit range and roughly a thousand times the measured error -- and the spot checks rel 1e-9, the double-precision contract. The `branch` column is the Fortran's cldfra1_flag and is exact. Assertions: Linf_error of the whole cldfra and branch columns against the inline reference, plus spot checks of cldfra at every layer the scheme returns a strictly fractional value for. Regime: the supercell's ice-and-snow anvil, longwave call 396, tile column 40. 38 condensate layers, every one pure ice, and the deepest fractional structure of the five: 30 strictly fractional layers running from 0.012 at the anvil edge to 0.998 in its core, five saturated layers and one layer that hits the -6.9 exponential floor, with three more snapped to zero by the 0.01 threshold. Together with supercell_warm_liquid this pins the two endpoints of the phase blend against a column that is not the SCM's.",
